    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1409">

                <pb facs="1368" n="1358" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1358"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/11–2549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Taipei</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Macdonald</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-25T17:00:00+08:00">November 25,
                            1949—5 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 25—7:01 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>745. ReDeptel 483, November 23, 7 p. m. Oral warnings continue as opportunity
                    permits. Americans’ reaction negative. No immediate departures expected.</p>
                <p>American official reaction to Deptel 446 similar except in case of those
                    previously caught on mainland none of whom should in our opinion remain here for
                    second “liberation”. Does Department contemplate replacing female employees
                    here?</p>
                <p>Sent Department 745, repeated Manila unnumbered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Macdonald</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
